  "title": "Week of October 24 — NVIDIA's Solar Throne Solidified, Amidst the Maelstrom of Volatility",
  "summary": "NVIDIA maintained the Solar Throne at $5.09 trillion, widening its gap with Apple, marking a week of notable upswings for Tesla and SpaceX.",
  "body": "<h3>Order in the Solar System, Between Stability and Vigilance</h3><p>The highest power in the universe remained unchanged last week. NVIDIA held the Solar position with a market cap of $5.09 trillion, and its gap with Apple ($5.07 trillion) actually widened. Microsoft ($3.89 trillion), Alphabet ($3.88 trillion), and Amazon ($2.67 trillion) followed, with the top five planetary arrangement maintaining a stable orbit without major shifts.</p><p>However, movements across the solar system were anything but tranquil. During the same period, severe declines were observed among some top-ranked planets. Meta Platforms suffered the week's steepest fall with a -9.4% decline, while Alphabet recorded -5.8% and JPMorgan Chase posted -2.4%.</p><h3>Rise of New Stars</h3><p>Within the declining universe, there were planets moving against the tide. Tesla emerged as the week's hottest planet with a +5.1% gain, followed by SpaceX with a +4.2% rise. Exxon Mobil also posted a +2.4% gain, with these three planets forming a weekly boom faction.</p><h3>Emerging Forces Beyond the Horizon</h3><p>Meanwhile, SK Hynix and Intel, classified as potential observation targets, have begun attracting market attention, while Sandisk (momentum 641), Dell (196), and MediaTek (193) are accumulating strong upward momentum. Though not yet among the solar system's uppermost ranks, they carry the potential to influence future reordering of the universe's structure.</p><p>The recorded universe proves itself through its very motion. The universe turns, and records remain.</p><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#9c7a3a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#f2ba3c\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"700\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#10141f\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#f2ba3c\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"800\">This Week's Stars — Burning and Dimming</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"56\" fill=\"#8a94b8\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-weight=\"600\">Earth TOP 20 Weekly Market Cap Change Rankings</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"95\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Tesla</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"80\" width=\"206\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"416\" y=\"95\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+5.1%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">SpaceX</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"113\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"380\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+4.2%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"161\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Exxon Mobil</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"146\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"307\" y=\"161\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+2.4%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Meta Platforms (</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"178\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"590\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-9.4%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Alphabet (Google</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"211\" width=\"234\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"444\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-5.8%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"259\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">JPMorgan Chase</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"244\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"307\" y=\"259\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-2.4%</text><text x=\"674\" y=\"296\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#9c7a3a\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"800\">UNIVERTRIX · univertrix.com</text></svg></div><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/20